<title>HONG KONG: Cheung Kong land bank to last to 2001.</title>
<headline>Cheung Kong land bank to last to 2001.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cheung Kong (Holdings) Ltd said on Wednesday its land bank could last until at least 2001.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect...our land bank can last for the coming four to five years,&quot; chairman Li Ka-shing told a news conference after the company released its 1996 results.</p>
<p>He pledged the firm would continue to expand its land bank and expected to pay HK$10 billion in land premiums from now until the end of 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;From this moment on, I estimate, to the end of this year, land premium will be over HK$10 billion,&quot; Li said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
